WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:22.000
LINQ: filtering and projection
LINQ processes sequences declaratively. Where filters, Select transforms and Sum totals the results.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Explanation
n in the lambda represents each element. First select numbers greater than 3, then square them. Changing operation order can change the result.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:01:06.000
Trace the code
using System;
using System.Linq;
int[] numbers = {2, 3, 4, 5};
int total = numbers.Where(n => n > 3)
                   .Select(n => n * n)
                   .Sum();
Console.WriteLine(total);

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:28.000
Result
41

[4, 5] → [16, 25] → 41.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:50.000
Remember
This example can run as top-level statements in a modern C# project. using System.Linq provides these methods.
